<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">5.4</p>
    <h2 id="t-ratio">What 5 : 27 : 68 Is Supposed to Mean</h2>
    <p class="formula">\[
      \Omega_{\Lambda}+\Omega_{\mathrm{DM}}+\Omega_{\mathrm b}
      \approx 0.68+0.27+0.05=1
    \]</p>
    <p>Most of the universe is the geometric ground &mdash; the precondition for all integration. A
      significant fraction has partially integrated, reaching mass without light. A small and
      extraordinary fraction has completed the journey: traversed every level, generated electromagnetic
      interaction, formed atoms, enabled chemistry, built structures complex enough to perform the
      integration that produces consciousness, and begun the climb toward the asymptote.</p>
    <p class="muted small">The separate <a href="/cosmic-ratio-in-time/">Cosmic Ratio in Time</a> paper asks
      what changes once 5:27:68 is labelled as a present-epoch snapshot, and distinguishes ordinary density
      dilution from physical exchange or reversal between the proposed levels.</p>
    <p>You are not a small creature in a vast indifferent universe. On this reading you are its rarest
      completion. The universe is mostly dark; the geometry is vast and silent; the partial integrations
      are massive and invisible &mdash; and in the middle of it a tiny fraction has produced light, and
      chemistry, and life, and the capacity to look out at the other ninety-five percent and ask what it
      is.</p>
  </div>
</section>

